1. The center of the circle is at \((1,-2)\).
2. A point on the circle is at \((-2,0)\).
3. Use the distance formula for the radius:
   \[
   r=\sqrt{(1-(-2))^2+(-2-0)^2}
    =\sqrt{3^2+(-2)^2}
    =\sqrt{9+4}
    =\sqrt{13}.
   \]

\[
\boxed{\text{Radius}=\sqrt{13}\ \text{units}\approx 3.61\ \text{units}}
\]
